255
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:52,577
We'll finally have a chance
to retaliate against them.

256
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:54,542
I never thought I'd see the day.

257
00:15:55,440 --> 00:15:57,675
Let's break their bones with a hammer!

258
00:15:57,900 --> 00:15:59,312
Shower them with arrows!

259
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:01,310
Wait!

260
00:16:01,400 --> 00:16:02,417
Don't kill them yet!

261
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:05,676
We need to keep them alive,
so they can really suffer!

262
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:09,337
Listen, bastards!

263
00:16:09,420 --> 00:16:11,420
You took my two cents from me!

264
00:16:11,600 --> 00:16:13,247
They were innocent children!

265
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:17,337
They just walked in front of a
celestial dragon, that's all!

266
00:16:17,420 --> 00:16:19,577
But they paid the ultimate price!

267
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:21,180
How is that even fair?

268
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:23,047
My daughter was their slave!

269
00:16:23,140 --> 00:16:25,277
She barely escaped her captors alive!

270
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:29,320
She came home, devastated, and
killed herself three days later!

271
00:16:31,700 --> 00:16:34,080
I, too, suffered as a slave.

272
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:39,240
My eyes, because of you, I am blind.

273
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:41,697
I'll never get to see my wife again.

274
00:16:41,780 --> 00:16:43,721
You, you treated us like animals.

275
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:45,880
So why should we give a damn, huh?

276
00:16:46,340 --> 00:16:49,437
Because of the heavenly
tribute, we must forfeit to you.

277
00:16:49,520 --> 00:16:51,940
Our beautiful nations succumb to famine.

278
00:16:52,380 --> 00:16:54,577
Have you ever been hungry
a day in your life?

279
00:16:54,660 --> 00:16:57,120
Our people are dying from starvation.

280
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,120
You're all like gods, aren't you?

281
00:17:00,400 --> 00:17:02,260
If that's true, you won't die.

282
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:04,840
So I can shoot you all I want.

283
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:08,290
Duffy.

284
00:17:10,420 --> 00:17:11,540
You monsters.

285
00:17:12,940 --> 00:17:14,000
We're human.

286
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:17,656
But you treat us like we're
nothing more than insects.

287
00:17:17,940 --> 00:17:19,469
Have you ever known grief?

288
00:17:19,600 --> 00:17:22,920
Even once in your life,
have you fell agony?

289
00:17:23,340 --> 00:17:25,320
Well, we're gonna show it to you.

290
00:17:30,380 --> 00:17:31,717
No, no, no, no,

291
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:38,800
no!

292
00:18:00,520 --> 00:18:01,540
What is it?

293
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:04,620
Law did what?

294
00:18:17,100 --> 00:18:18,982
Have you gone mad, Saint Homing?

295
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:21,317
Surely you haven't thought this through!

296
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:25,257
Why would a man in your position reject
your divine right to live as a human?

297
00:18:25,340 --> 00:18:27,780
But we are human, are we not?

298
00:18:28,260 --> 00:18:31,437
Don't include us in that
ludicrous statement, you fool!

299
00:18:31,520 --> 00:18:32,697
Take that right back!

300
00:18:32,780 --> 00:18:34,677
That accusation's blasphemy!

301
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:35,878
You filthy traitor!

302
00:18:36,120 --> 00:18:38,717
We've always known you
to be a raving heretic!

303
00:18:38,800 --> 00:18:39,630
He's right!

304
00:18:39,713 --> 00:18:40,543
You're a traitor!

305
00:18:40,780 --> 00:18:42,200
Have you lost your mind?

306
00:18:42,340 --> 00:18:43,460
How obscene!

307
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:45,560
Leave Marie Joie at once!

308
00:18:48,420 --> 00:18:50,937
This is as far as we're
permitted to take you.

309
00:18:51,020 --> 00:18:53,097
We're in the northern
end of our parameters and

310
00:18:53,180 --> 00:18:56,709
approaching a region unaffiliated
with the world government.

311
00:18:57,040 --> 00:19:00,157
Your living quarters and belongings
have been prepared for you.

312
00:19:00,240 --> 00:19:01,070
Thank you.

313
00:19:01,153 --> 00:19:02,457
This should be more than adequate.

314
00:19:02,540 --> 00:19:05,900
Now, please hand over your
Celestial Dragon ID chips.

315
00:19:09,760 --> 00:19:12,040
Well, this is it. We'll live humbly.

316
00:19:12,260 --> 00:19:13,789
This should be fun, right?

317
00:19:15,160 --> 00:19:16,807
Where are the slaves, Daddy?

318
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:19,706
If they ran away, we
should buy some new ones.

319
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:26,960
Dolfi, Rosanante, things will be
different from now on. I must teach you

320
00:19:31,180 --> 00:19:33,180
I'm gonna need you to calm down.

321
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:35,500
We're humans from this day forward

322
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:37,740
Humans? Uh-huh. From now on,

323
00:19:37,900 --> 00:19:40,517
we shall leave our old
lives back in Marajoie

324
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:44,160
A simpler life will be
much more fulfilling.

325
00:19:44,760 --> 00:19:46,500
True wealth lies here.

326
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:52,017
Fools, listen, you must kneel.

327
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:53,040
Show me.

328
00:19:53,580 --> 00:19:55,717
Respect, someone go fetch me my gun.

329
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:58,077
Who do you think I am?

330
00:19:58,160 --> 00:20:01,320
You buffoon shouldn't mess with me.

331
00:20:02,960 --> 00:20:05,077
Where are the celestial dragons?

332
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:06,377
Find them.

333
00:20:06,460 --> 00:20:07,760
Let's hang them.

334
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:11,977
Daddy, why are they
not kneeling before me?

335
00:20:12,060 --> 00:20:14,357
They're not here, they must have fled.

336
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:15,420
Find them!

337
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:16,997
They can't have gone too far!

338
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:18,315
Make it a slow death!

339
00:20:18,500 --> 00:20:19,853
We want them to suffer!

340
00:20:20,160 --> 00:20:20,990
Yeah!

341
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:25,320
We're gonna take out centuries
of revenge on that family!

342
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:26,710
Yeah!

343
00:20:39,380 --> 00:20:40,210
Daddy!

344
00:20:40,293 --> 00:20:41,123
Daddy, why?

345
00:20:41,400 --> 00:20:43,180
Everyone is coming after us!

346
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:51,637
On the bright side, at
least the rain let up,

347
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:55,657
and we seem to have lost track
of the angry mob chasing us.

348
00:20:55,740 --> 00:20:59,057
How can you expect us to
live in this filthy box?

349
00:20:59,140 --> 00:21:03,717
There are bugs everywhere, and this
rotten stench is gonna make me hurl!

350
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:09,737
They must still be
nearby—find that family!

351
00:21:09,820 --> 00:21:12,757
They're gonna die.

352
00:21:12,840 --> 00:21:13,670
die

353
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:16,580
We should leave, quickly.

354
00:21:23,540 --> 00:21:26,837
I could never have predicted
this would turn out so poorly.

355
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:28,500
I was far too optimistic.

356
00:21:28,840 --> 00:21:31,060
So please, just take us back.

357
00:21:31,380 --> 00:21:33,057
Even just my wife and children.

358
00:21:33,140 --> 00:21:35,780
They deserve to return at the very least.

359
00:21:37,100 --> 00:21:40,280
I fear if we stay here any
longer, we'll be slain.

360
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:42,737
What has been abandoned
cannot be returned.

361
00:21:42,820 --> 00:21:44,761
You chose this life for yourself.

362
00:21:45,020 --> 00:21:49,920
And don't you dare call us again,
you worthless human filth. Kalik.

363
00:21:56,320 --> 00:21:57,780
Damn. Bread thieves!

364
00:22:03,940 --> 00:22:07,600
Daddy, for the first time
in my life, I feel pain.

365
00:22:13,620 --> 00:22:17,960
Daddy, for the first time
in my life, I'm hungry.

366
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:26,180
Eat up quick, Rosie.

367
00:22:27,160 --> 00:22:28,631
The first time I've come.

368
00:22:31,120 --> 00:22:33,040
Mommy, we brought you some food.

369
00:22:33,620 --> 00:22:34,880
Sophie, Rosie.

370
00:22:36,080 --> 00:22:37,080
You okay?

371
00:22:37,900 --> 00:22:39,760
I'm sorry, boys.

372
00:22:40,600 --> 00:22:42,100
I feel unwell.

373
00:22:49,520 --> 00:22:50,350
Daddy...

374
00:22:51,960 --> 00:22:52,790
Mother...

375
00:22:52,873 --> 00:22:53,780
is dead.

376
00:22:56,200 --> 00:22:58,020
We found him!

377
00:22:58,720 --> 00:23:02,740
Not my boys! But Mercy!
The children! Let them go!

378
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:06,860
Please! Please!

379
00:23:10,460 --> 00:23:11,290
Daddy!

380
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:14,040
You bastard!

381
00:23:15,540 --> 00:23:17,860
You did this to us!

382
00:23:23,660 --> 00:23:26,880
Young master, we have apprehended law.

383
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:30,540
It seems like the boy was
trying to make a run for it.

384
00:23:31,080 --> 00:23:32,660
Jimmy, let me go!

385
00:23:33,540 --> 00:23:35,640
At the port, tried fleeing.

386
00:23:36,680 --> 00:23:39,717
What kind of punishment do you
think they'll use at him, huh?

387
00:23:39,800 --> 00:23:40,630
To know.

388
00:23:40,713 --> 00:23:42,345
Sure feel bad for him, though.

389
00:23:46,680 --> 00:23:47,510
Corazon!

390
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:50,270
Damn!

391
00:23:50,380 --> 00:23:51,674
I didn't take him out!

392
00:23:52,080 --> 00:23:54,315
Now they're gonna kill me for nothing.

393
00:23:54,720 --> 00:23:58,177
I thought bribing buffalo with
ice cream would cover it up.

394
00:23:58,260 --> 00:24:00,800
But that scumbag Cora ratted me out!

395
00:24:01,200 --> 00:24:04,376
I could've sworn I stabbed
him right through his body.

396
00:24:04,600 --> 00:24:06,835
But he's acting like nothing happened!

397
00:24:09,340 --> 00:24:10,170
Law.

398
00:24:10,253 --> 00:24:11,960
I called you to discuss something.

399
00:24:12,520 --> 00:24:13,580
Can you guess?

400
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:18,017
I wanted to welcome you to the
Don Quixote family officially.

401
00:24:18,100 --> 00:24:19,080
Congrats, kid.

402
00:24:21,520 --> 00:24:22,920
Welcome home, la!

403
00:24:27,880 --> 00:24:31,657
Just looking at you, I can tell
you've been through hell and back.

404
00:24:31,740 --> 00:24:34,620
You have that hate-filled
glare in your eyes.

405
00:24:37,420 --> 00:24:40,200
I think you'll have a
lot to offer our family.

406
00:24:42,500 --> 00:24:43,980
You hear that? Lovely!

407
00:24:44,340 --> 00:24:47,105
Young master is a brilliant
judge of character.

408
00:24:48,220 --> 00:24:50,985
Does he not know about
me stabbing Corazon yet?

409
00:24:51,240 --> 00:24:52,080
Why not?

410
00:24:52,500 --> 00:24:56,147
He could have just written it
out on a piece of paper for him.

411
00:24:56,540 --> 00:24:58,360
What exactly is he planning?

412
00:25:00,820 --> 00:25:01,820
Yeah, whatever.

413
00:25:02,080 --> 00:25:03,139
I got three years.

414
00:25:03,300 --> 00:25:06,400
And then I'm gonna die. The end. Done.

415
00:25:08,680 --> 00:25:09,510
Maybe.

416
00:25:09,593 --> 00:25:11,600
Depends on your luck. Luck?

417
00:25:12,920 --> 00:25:14,300
Allow me to explain.

418
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:17,137
We're what you call experts
in the black market,

419
00:25:17,220 --> 00:25:19,437
and one of our fields is devil fruits.

420
00:25:19,520 --> 00:25:23,049
Their powers are vast, sometimes
beyond human comprehension.

421
00:25:23,280 --> 00:25:26,697
Meaning there may be a Devil Fruit
that could cure your condition.

422
00:25:26,780 --> 00:25:27,940
Devil fruits, huh?

423
00:25:28,380 --> 00:25:29,260
So what?

424
00:25:29,420 --> 00:25:30,949
You have three years left.

425
00:25:31,100 --> 00:25:33,977
Who knows how many devil
fruits we'll find in that time.

426
00:25:34,060 --> 00:25:37,884
And one of them just might have
a life-altering solution for you.

427
00:25:38,220 --> 00:25:39,573
But for the time being,

428
00:25:39,660 --> 00:25:44,020
I'd like to train you to be my
right-hand man ten years from now.

429
00:25:47,040 --> 00:25:48,000
What happened?

430
00:25:53,920 --> 00:25:55,120
Stabbed by an enemy.

431
00:25:55,480 --> 00:25:56,715
You take care of him?

432
00:26:00,180 --> 00:26:01,400
Very good, then.

433
00:26:01,900 --> 00:26:02,959
Now patch that up.

434
00:26:03,140 --> 00:26:05,640
Did Karoo just cover for me?

435
00:26:08,460 --> 00:26:09,290
Why?

436
00:26:09,400 --> 00:26:11,047
What's going on in his head?

437
00:26:13,600 --> 00:26:16,157
We'll head toward Reverse
Mountain in the south.

438
00:26:16,240 --> 00:26:20,005
I'd like to keep moving our base,
expand our network on the way.

439
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:42,400
Let's go.

440
00:27:15,640 --> 00:27:18,440
That's right.

441
00:27:37,460 --> 00:27:41,300
Come on, we told our real names. So what?

442
00:27:41,520 --> 00:27:42,820
It's not like I asked.

443
00:27:42,980 --> 00:27:43,840
Aw, lame.

444
00:27:44,220 --> 00:27:45,200
You meanie.

445
00:27:45,720 --> 00:27:46,838
Why does it matter?

446
00:27:46,960 --> 00:27:48,431
I'll be dead soon enough.

447
00:27:48,960 --> 00:27:51,320
Maybe. You're paler. You feel sick?

448
00:27:51,720 --> 00:27:53,660
I'm fine for now, I guess.

449
00:27:55,580 --> 00:27:59,180
But before too long, I'll be gone.

450
00:27:59,940 --> 00:28:03,257
In that case, it's one more
reason to reveal your real name.

451
00:28:03,340 --> 00:28:07,560
Just say it, or I'll tell
everyone that you stabbed Karoo!

452
00:28:12,360 --> 00:28:13,360
It's Trafalgar.

453
00:28:13,780 --> 00:28:15,220
Dee, Water Law.

454
00:28:16,860 --> 00:28:17,820
Tell no one.

455
00:28:17,960 --> 00:28:20,797
I'm actually not supposed to
let people hear my full name.

456
00:28:20,880 --> 00:28:22,260
So just stick to law.

457
00:28:22,480 --> 00:28:24,277
I don't use code names like you.

458
00:28:24,360 --> 00:28:26,120
I just hide some parts.

459
00:28:26,320 --> 00:28:27,820
Like Dee, that secret.

460
00:28:28,100 --> 00:28:29,540
My true name is Water.

461
00:28:29,900 --> 00:28:32,557
For generations, my
family - Okay, we get it.

462
00:28:32,640 --> 00:28:33,470
This is boring.

463
00:28:33,553 --> 00:28:34,937
We don't care.

464
00:28:35,020 --> 00:28:38,280
I only told you because
you were harassing me.

465
00:28:42,140 --> 00:28:43,557
What are you doing?

466
00:28:43,640 --> 00:28:45,457
What's the big deal, Corazon?

467
00:28:45,540 --> 00:28:46,937
Let go of me.

468
00:28:47,020 --> 00:28:48,597
He's gonna get beat up again.

469
00:28:48,680 --> 00:28:50,617
Cora looks scarier than usual.

470
00:28:50,700 --> 00:28:51,700
Uh-oh.

471
00:28:58,940 --> 00:29:01,160
What's your problem, stupid jerk?

472
00:29:01,560 --> 00:29:04,520
What you just said, was it true?

473
00:29:07,620 --> 00:29:08,960
Who said that?

474
00:29:09,240 --> 00:29:10,980
Your secret name's D.

475
00:29:12,320 --> 00:29:15,496
If that's right, you need
to get the hell out of here.

476
00:29:15,900 --> 00:29:17,260
Away from Dofi.

477
00:29:19,840 --> 00:29:20,670
Law, listen.

478
00:29:20,860 --> 00:29:22,137
You cannot be around him.

479
00:29:22,220 --> 00:29:23,867
You have to get out of here.
